<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 115 0 R/E(12)/Pg 21 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

476 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 115 0 R/T(Meet the Villager: Derek Hadlow)/E(Meet the Villager: Derek Hadlow)/Pg 21 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

477 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 115 0 R/T(A lifetime in Broomfield)/E(A lifetime in Broomfield)/Pg 21 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

478 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 115 0 R/E(At 83, Derek Hadlow has a lifetime of memories to share about Broomfield. Born here in 1943, he has witnessed enormous changes over the years. Having served as verger at St Margaret\220s Church since 1971, Derek has dedicated 55 years to caring for this special part of the community.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

479 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 115 0 R/T(Growing Up in Broomfield)/E(Growing Up in Broomfield)/Pg 21 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

480 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 115 0 R/E(Derek was born at No. 2 Upper Street and christened at St Margaret\220s Church, just across the road. Life was very different then, with no indoor toilet and baths taken in a tin bath!)/Pg 21 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

481 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 115 0 R/E(He remembers a happy childhood playing cricket and football in the road with friends and racing around in homemade soapbox carts. There was so little traffic that he recalls seeing just two cars in a week! He also remembers walking to school and crossing a bridge near Broomfield that was demolished around the 1950s.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

482 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 115 0 R/T(Memories of Leeds Castle)/E(Memories of Leeds Castle)/Pg 21 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

483 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 115 0 R/E(Derek worked in farming and gardening, following in his father\220s footsteps. His father worked at Church Farm before becoming a gardener, and Derek also spent time working at Leeds Castle.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

484 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 115 0 R/E(He fondly remembers Lady Baillie as a good employer who looked after her staff. She loved birds and gardening, and the castle had 14 greenhouses where peaches and flowers were grown. One Christmas, they even had to adapt an enormous Christmas tree to make it fit inside the Castle!)/Pg 21 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

485 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 116 0 R/Pg 22 0 R/A[1335 0 R 0]/K[0]>>
endobj

486 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 116 0 R/Pg 22 0 R/A[1336 0 R 0]/K[1]>>
endobj

487 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(13)/Pg 22 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

488 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(Would you like to be featured in \217Meet the Villager\220?)/Pg 22 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

489 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E( I\220d love to hear your story. )/Pg 22 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

490 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(Contact me at pauline.silk@hotmail.co.uk or 07917 105460.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

491 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(Thank you, Derek, for sharing your memories and helping us discover more about the history of Broomfield.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

492 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(Devoted to St Margaret\220s Church)/Pg 22 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

493 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(In 1971, Derek became verger because he felt the village church needed someone to care for it. The churchyard was badly overgrown, with grass reaching the height of the gravestones.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

494 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(Since then, Derek has helped prepare for services, weddings and funerals, cared for the churchyard, rung the bells and created beautiful floral displays. He remains proud of the church and its traditions, despite the changes in village life.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

495 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(Family and Village History)/Pg 22 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

496 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(Derek shared some wonderful old photographs of his family and villagers gathered on the church green. Several generations of his family have lived locally, making Broomfield part of his story throughout his life.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

497 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(He also devoted more than 40 years to caring for his sister after she became paralysed. Today, he still enjoys gardening and has kept old church magazines and photographs that offer a fascinating glimpse into the village\220s past.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

498 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(With 55 years of service to St Margaret\220s Church and a lifetime of memories, Derek is a wonderful link to Broomfield\220s history. )/Pg 22 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

