550 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 123 0 R/E(That should mean a hard \217no\220 for the 8,400 houses proposed for Highsted Park near Sittingbourne. )/Pg 29 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

551 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 123 0 R/E(But the change of Prime Minister means a change of Secretaries of State \205 and that decision will now be made by the current Housing Secretary, Angela Rayner, in November. I am working with local councillors and campaigners to persuade her to refuse the application.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

552 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 123 0 R/E(Thank you to everyone who has supported my campaign to get the Government to think again about the volume of houses being imposed on rural Kent. I know we need more homes, but it simply doesn't make sense to build 20,000 more houses on greenfield sites meanwhile brownfield sites in London and other towns are left undeveloped. )/Pg 29 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

553 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 123 0 R/E(If you agree with me, please give me your backing by signing my Halt the Houses petition at www.HaltTheHouses.com. )/Pg 29 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

554 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 123 0 R/E(Best wishes)/Pg 29 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

555 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 123 0 R/E(Helen)/Pg 29 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

556 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 123 0 R/E(20)/Pg 29 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

557 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 123 0 R/T(Update from Helen Whately MP)/E(Update from Helen Whately MP)/Pg 29 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

558 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 123 0 R/E(Helen Whately MP taking her 7,000 strong \217Stop the Sprawl\220 petition to Downing Street for the direct attention of the Prime Minister. She is now applying for a debate in Parliament to keep the pressure on Ministers to reduce our housing numbers.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

559 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 123 0 R/E(This summer, Kent was officially classified as being in drought.  We've had a hosepipe ban virtually all year round and multiple major water outages. Water is being tankered along narrow country lanes just to keep our taps flowing. )/Pg 29 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

560 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 123 0 R/E(The fact is, we don't have enough water to supply the current population of this area, let alone thousands more houses. There are 20,000 new houses proposed for Faversham and Mid Kent alone.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

561 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 123 0 R/E(Don't just take my word for it. South East Water has said publicly there's not enough water for development planned in neighbouring areas like Tonbridge and Malling. I'm waiting for their judgement on the houses planned for Maidstone and Swale. )/Pg 29 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

562 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 123 0 R/E(There is a new Kent reservoir coming but it won\220t be operational until the mid-2030s at the earliest. )/Pg 29 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

563 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 123 0 R/E(In the summer, the housing secretary at the time \(Steve Reed MP\) told BBC South East that new homes \215will not be built\216 if the infrastructure to provide them with water is not in place.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

